This repository is the Areneon fork of that project (https://github.com/piglor/ninjask).
The fork keeps the licence and this notice, and the upstream copyright stays with its
authors. What the fork changes (CHANGELOG.md, "0.4.1+areneon.0"): it is pinned to a
later Pokémon Showdown commit than upstream's, with that commit's Champions No Retreat
behaviour ported; Revival Blessing's forced-switch choices are enumerated as Showdown
accepts them; the data exports verify the Showdown checkout they come from and record a
hash of every handler's source; refsim/PROVENANCE.json records the exports and
docs/repin.md is the procedure for a pin bump. Its Python distribution is named
ninjask-areneon (the import name stays ninjask). Upstream contributions are welcome
but not required.

Pokémon Showdown
----------------
https://github.com/smogon/pokemon-showdown, commit 7244fe8e28fa8bc4d0809ae30d183c608b62bb2b
(refsim/SHOWDOWN_COMMIT; upstream Ninjask was pinned to 3a766f2cfb5e51c1e428cfe87d0dba91a8f01640)

The engine's battle logic is a port of Pokémon Showdown's (the Champions mod
and the base game it builds on): damage calculation, the action queue, move,
ability, item and condition handlers, the choice syntax, the protocol log
format and the random number generator. The data the engine loads (species,
moves, abilities, items, learnsets, natures, the type chart and format rules)
is exported from the same commit by refsim/export_format.js. Pokémon Showdown
is also run as the reference simulator by the checks in scripts/, but is not
part of this repository: scripts/setup_showdown.sh clones it into
third_party/. Its license:

